hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"348","[AI-translation] Hamain Ahmed bin 'Abdah Ad-Dabbi ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Fudail bin 'Iyaz ne hadith ki, Mansoor se, Zuhri se, 'Urwah se, 'Aishah se, unhon ne kaha: Maine Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) ko apni mazlumah ka intiqam liye hue kabhi nahi dekha, jab tak ke Allah Ta'ala ke muharramat mein se koi cheez na chidi ho, aur jab Allah ke muharramat mein se koi cheez chidi toh wo is mein sab se zyada ghusse wala hota, aur jab unhein do mamilon mein se ikhtiyar diya jata toh aasan tar ko muntakhib farmate, jab tak ke wo koi gunah na ho."
"349","[AI-translation] Hamain Ibn Abi 'Umar ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Sufyan ne hadith ki, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir se, 'Urwah se, 'Aishah se, unhon ne kaha: Ek shakhs ne Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) se ijazat talab ki, aur main unke paas thi, toh farmaya: Bura hai kabeelay ka beta ya kabeelay ka bhai. Phir usay ijazat di, toh uske saath narmi se kaha. Jab wo nikal gaya, toh maine kaha: Ya Rasool Allah! Aapne jo farmaya phir uske saath narmi se kaha? Farmaya: Ya 'Aishah! Logon mein se bad-tareen shakhs wo hai jise log chhor dein ya us se ijtenaab karein us ki bad-zabani se darte hue."
"350","[AI-translation] Hamain Sufyan bin Waki' ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Jama' bin 'Umar bin 'Abdir-Rahman Al-'Ijli ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamein Bani Tamim se, Abu Halah (zoj-e-Khadijah) ki aulaad mein se, ek aadmi ne khabar di, jinki kuniyat Abu 'Abdullah hai, Abu Halah ke ek bete se, Hasan bin 'Ali se, unhon ne kaha: Husain ne kaha: Maine apne waalid se Nabi (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) ke jalsa-e-majalis ke siwah (sirat o akhlaq) ke baray mein sawal kiya, toh farmaya: Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) hamesha muskuraye rehte, khulq ke saath narm, lenaay ke saath naram, na fazz aur na ghaleez, na shor karnay wale na fahash, na aib lagnay wale na shohrat talab. Jo cheez pasand na ho us se ghaffel rehte, aur umeed wale ko na umeed karte aur na mayoos karte. Apni taraf se teen cheezein chhor di: be-faida jhagra, boht bolna, aur jo unhein matlub na ho. Aur logon ki taraf se teen cheezein chhor di: kisi ko burai nahi karte, na aib lagate, aur na us ka aib talash karte. Na bolte magar us mein jis ka sawab umeed ho, aur jab bolte toh jalsay wale sar jhuka kar sunte goya unke saron par parinde baithe hon. Aur jab khamosh ho jate toh bolte, unke paas hadis par jhagra nahi karte. Aur jo unke paas bolta, usey khatam hone tak chup rehte. Un ka hadith unke paas pehlay ki tarah hota, jis par wo hanste us par hanste, aur jis cheez se ajeeb karte us se ajeeb karte. Ajnabi ke kath zabaani aur sawal par sabr karte, yahan tak ke unke ashab bhi, aur farmate: Jab koi zaroorat mand ko dekho jo sawal kare toh usay aita karo (madad karo). Sifat (tareef) qubool nahi karte magar aisay shakhs ki jo muqabla karta ho. Aur kisi ki hadis par abha nahi karte yahan tak ke khul jaye, phir mana karne ya utth jane se chhor dete."
"351","[AI-translation] Hamain Muhammad bin Bashshar ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain 'Abdur Rahman bin Mahdi ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Sufyan ne hadith ki, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir se, farmaya: Maine Jabir bin 'Abdullah ko farmate hue suna: Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) se kabhi koi cheez mangi nahi gayi aur unhone na kaha."
"352","[AI-translation] Hamain 'Abdullah bin 'Imran Abu Al-Qasim Al-Qurashi Al-Makki ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Ibrahim bin Sa'd ne hadith ki, Ibn Shihab se, 'Ubaidullah se, Ibn 'Abbas se, unhon ne kaha: Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) khair mein logon mein sab se zyada sakhi the, aur Ramzan ke mahine mein sab se zyada sakhi hote, yahan tak ke (mahina) guzar jaye. Toh unhein Jibril aate, aur Quran un par arz karte. Toh jab Jibril se mulaqat hoti toh Rasool Allah (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) khair mein behati hui hawa se bhi zyada sakhi hote."
"353","[AI-translation] Hamain Qutaibah bin Sa'id ne hadith ki, farmaya: Hamain Ja'far bin Sulaiman ne khabar di, Thabit se, Anas bin Malik se, unhon ne kaha: Nabi (sallallahu alayhi wasallam) kal ke liye kuch bacha kar nahi rakhte the."
